wmcube: reads every pending event, not one per frame

The event loop ends with a "break" that leaves the while (XPending) loop
after the first event, so wmcube handled one event per frame (10 ms plus
the drawing). The dock-app asks for pointer motion: a mouse moving over
it at 125-1000 Hz piles up motion events, and a click waited behind
them. Measured in a nested wlmaker (X11 dock-app on XWayland), after 2 s
of motion over the tile: the object changed 522-679 ms after the click,
or not within 5 s at 500 Hz. With every pending event read: 105 ms at
125, 500 and 1000 Hz (the measurement's floor).

diff --git a/wmcube/wmcube/wmcube.c b/wmcube/wmcube/wmcube.c
index 3d51247..7a4ebd4 100644
--- a/wmcube/wmcube/wmcube.c
+++ b/wmcube/wmcube/wmcube.c
@@ -384,7 +384,8 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
 							break;
 					}
 			}	
-			break;
+			/* every pending event, not one per frame: the pointer motion
+			 * of a fast mouse piled up and a click waited for seconds */
 		}
 		usleep(screen_speed);
 	}
